      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/c2452160f8af4651bdc78756b7c0df8402de185ba7a7bedbc1c1a676b342af97.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14245698/assets/eea68ab4e4b440609fcc4f6c2d40c4dc9fc394fc45f1047ec9c658729322749a.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the parabola ${y}^{2}=4x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}=4x\\,\\}.\n$$",
